  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/argument-from-analogy> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The presumptive argument pattern \"case C1 is similar to case C2; conclusion A holds in C1; so A plausibly holds in C2\". Its strength depends on whether the shared features are relevant to A, whether relevant differences undercut the comparison, and whether a rival analogy points the other way." .
