  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/argument-from-expert-opinion> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The presumptive argument pattern \"E is an expert in domain S, which contains claim A; E asserts A; so A may plausibly be accepted\". It is reasonable but defeasible: its strength depends on answers to critical questions about the expert's competence, field, statement, reliability, agreement with other experts and evidence." .
