  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/dialectic> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Reasoning conducted as an exchange between opposing positions, classically a disciplined question-and-answer contest in which a questioner tries to draw a respondent's concessions into contradiction; the term later also named formal logic (Stoics, medieval schools), Kant's critique of reason overreaching itself, Hegel's account of concepts developing through their own contradictions, and today's dialogue-based theories of argument." .
