<https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/presumption#graph> {
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/presumption> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2026-11-12"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/presumption> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/ontology#Concept> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/presumption> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Presumption" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/presumption> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "praesumptio" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/presumption> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "presumptive status" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/presumption> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "rebuttable presumption" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/presumption> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/argument-evaluation> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/presumption> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The status a claim has when it may be accepted without proof for now, so that the burden of proof falls on anyone who would reject it; a presumption stands until it is rebutted, but it is always defeasible." .
