  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/hindsight-bias> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "knew-it-all-along effect" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/hindsight-bias> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/cognitive-bias> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/hindsight-bias> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The tendency, once an outcome is known, to judge it as having been more predictable, more inevitable and more obvious beforehand than it actually was, and to misremember one's earlier predictions as closer to the outcome." .
