  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/source-monitoring-framework> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "source attribution in memory" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/source-monitoring-framework> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "source monitoring" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/source-monitoring-framework> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/metacognition> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/source-monitoring-framework> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A model from memory research of how people decide where a thought, memory or feeling of familiarity came from (something seen, something read, something imagined). Because those decisions are inferences, they can fail, and deliberately checking the source of familiarity is a practical guard against mistaking \"I've heard of it\" for \"it is true, famous or important\"." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/source-monitoring-framework> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/scheme/debiasing-and-metacognition> .
