  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/expected-utility-theory> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The model of choice under risk that values each option by weighting the utility of its possible outcomes by their probabilities and recommends the option with the highest total; it is the classical normative standard for rational decisions and a much-criticised descriptive model of how people actually choose." .
