<https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/reversible-and-irreversible-decisions#graph> {
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/reversible-and-irreversible-decisions> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2026-11-07"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/reversible-and-irreversible-decisions> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/ontology#Concept> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/reversible-and-irreversible-decisions> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Reversible and irreversible decisions" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/reversible-and-irreversible-decisions> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Type 1 and Type 2 decisions" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/reversible-and-irreversible-decisions> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "decision reversibility" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/reversible-and-irreversible-decisions> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "one-way and two-way door decisions" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/reversible-and-irreversible-decisions> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/judgment-and-decision-making> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/reversible-and-irreversible-decisions> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The distinction between choices that can be cheaply undone once more is learned and choices that lock in their consequences; it sets how much deliberation, evidence and delay a decision deserves, and it also changes how people feel about a choice after making it." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/reversible-and-irreversible-decisions> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/scheme/decision-making> .
