  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/conflict-of-interest> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A set of circumstances that creates a substantial risk that a person's professional judgment about a primary interest (a patient's welfare, the validity of research, a client's outcome) will be unduly influenced by a secondary interest such as financial gain; it names a risk of bias, not proof that bias occurred, and it is a legitimate reason to seek independent evidence." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/conflict-of-interest> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/scheme/evidence-and-information-literacy> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/conflict-of-interest> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Conflict of interest" .
