  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/elaboration-likelihood-model> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A dual-process model of persuasion holding that people change their attitudes either by scrutinising the merits of a message's arguments (the central route) or by reacting to simple cues such as a source's expertise or likeability (the peripheral route), with motivation and ability to think deciding which route dominates." .
