<https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/affirming-a-disjunct#graph> {
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/affirming-a-disjunct/cq/1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/ontology#CriticalQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/affirming-a-disjunct/cq/1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Could both alternatives in the \"or\" premise be true at the same time?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/affirming-a-disjunct/cq/1> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/affirming-a-disjunct> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/affirming-a-disjunct/cq/2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/ontology#CriticalQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/affirming-a-disjunct/cq/2> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Is the \"or\" meant exclusively, and if so, has the \"not both\" claim been stated and supported?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/affirming-a-disjunct/cq/2> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/affirming-a-disjunct> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/affirming-a-disjunct/cq/3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/ontology#CriticalQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/affirming-a-disjunct/cq/3> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Does the affirmed alternative by itself rule out the other one, independent of the disjunction?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/affirming-a-disjunct/cq/3> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/affirming-a-disjunct> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/affirming-a-disjunct/cq/4> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/ontology#CriticalQuestion> .
