  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/denying-a-conjunct/cq/2> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Has anyone actually established that at least one of the two options must hold, or is that an unstated assumption?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/denying-a-conjunct/cq/2> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/denying-a-conjunct> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/denying-a-conjunct/cq/3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/ontology#CriticalQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/denying-a-conjunct/cq/3> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Does the denied conjunct, on its own, imply the conclusion regardless of the \"not both\" premise?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/denying-a-conjunct/cq/3> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/denying-a-conjunct> .
