<https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/exclusive-premises#graph> {
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/exclusive-premises/cq/1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/ontology#CriticalQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/exclusive-premises/cq/1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Are both premises negative, so that each one only says which things are excluded from the middle class?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/exclusive-premises/cq/1> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/exclusive-premises> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/exclusive-premises/cq/2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/ontology#CriticalQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/exclusive-premises/cq/2> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Does anything in the premises say how the conclusion's subject and predicate relate to each other directly?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/exclusive-premises/cq/2> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/exclusive-premises> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/exclusive-premises/cq/3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/ontology#CriticalQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/exclusive-premises/cq/3> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Can you describe a case where both premises are true and the conclusion is false?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/exclusive-premises/cq/3> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/exclusive-premises> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/exclusive-premises/cq/4> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/ontology#CriticalQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/exclusive-premises/cq/4> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Did the arguer mean a stronger affirmative claim, such as \"only X can do this\", that should be stated and defended?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/exclusive-premises/cq/4> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/exclusive-premises> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/exclusive-premises/map/c> <http://www.arg.dundee.ac.uk/aif#claimText> "No interns can approve expenses." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/exclusive-premises/map/c> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.arg.dundee.ac.uk/aif#I-node> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/exclusive-premises/map/ca1> <http://www.arg.dundee.ac.uk/aif#Conclusion> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/exclusive-premises/map/ra> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/exclusive-premises/map/ca1> <http://www.arg.dundee.ac.uk/aif#Premise> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/exclusive-premises/map/o1> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/exclusive-premises/map/ca1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.arg.dundee.ac.uk/aif#CA-node> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/exclusive-premises/map/ca2> <http://www.arg.dundee.ac.uk/aif#Conclusion> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/exclusive-premises/map/ra> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/exclusive-premises/map/ca2> <http://www.arg.dundee.ac.uk/aif#Premise> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/exclusive-premises/map/o2> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/exclusive-premises/map/ca2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.arg.dundee.ac.uk/aif#CA-node> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/exclusive-premises/map/o1> <http://www.arg.dundee.ac.uk/aif#claimText> "The premises only say who is outside the security team; an intern could still approve expenses through a project budget role." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/exclusive-premises/map/o1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.arg.dundee.ac.uk/aif#I-node> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/exclusive-premises/map/o2> <http://www.arg.dundee.ac.uk/aif#claimText> "Both premises would stay true even if every intern could approve expenses, so they cannot rule it out." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/exclusive-premises/map/o2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.arg.dundee.ac.uk/aif#I-node> .
