  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/exclusive-premises> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The syllogistic fallacy of drawing a conclusion from two negative premises. Because each premise only excludes one class from the middle term, the premises fix no relation between the conclusion's two terms, so every categorical syllogism with two negative premises is invalid." .
