<https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/existential-fallacy#graph> {
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/existential-fallacy/cq/1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/ontology#CriticalQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/existential-fallacy/cq/1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Do the premises say that anything in the subject class actually exists, or only what would be true of its members?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/existential-fallacy/cq/1> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/existential-fallacy> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/existential-fallacy/cq/2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/ontology#CriticalQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/existential-fallacy/cq/2> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Could the subject class be empty, as with a rule about cases that have not happened yet?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/existential-fallacy/cq/2> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/existential-fallacy> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/existential-fallacy/cq/3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/ontology#CriticalQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/existential-fallacy/cq/3> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "If the class is known to have members, has that existence premise been stated so the argument can be checked?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/existential-fallacy/cq/3> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/existential-fallacy> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/existential-fallacy/cq/4> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/ontology#CriticalQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/existential-fallacy/cq/4> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Does a Venn diagram of the premises place an X in the region the particular conclusion needs?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/existential-fallacy/cq/4> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/existential-fallacy> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/existential-fallacy/map/c> <http://www.arg.dundee.ac.uk/aif#claimText> "Some employees who beat their quota this quarter will be named in the newsletter." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/existential-fallacy/map/c> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.arg.dundee.ac.uk/aif#I-node> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/existential-fallacy/map/ca1> <http://www.arg.dundee.ac.uk/aif#Conclusion> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/existential-fallacy/map/ra> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/existential-fallacy/map/ca1> <http://www.arg.dundee.ac.uk/aif#Premise> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/existential-fallacy/map/o1> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/existential-fallacy/map/ca1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.arg.dundee.ac.uk/aif#CA-node> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/existential-fallacy/map/ca2> <http://www.arg.dundee.ac.uk/aif#Conclusion> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/existential-fallacy/map/ra> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/existential-fallacy/map/ca2> <http://www.arg.dundee.ac.uk/aif#Premise> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/existential-fallacy/map/o2> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/existential-fallacy/map/ca2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.arg.dundee.ac.uk/aif#CA-node> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/existential-fallacy/map/ca3> <http://www.arg.dundee.ac.uk/aif#Conclusion> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/existential-fallacy/map/ra> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/existential-fallacy/map/ca3> <http://www.arg.dundee.ac.uk/aif#Premise> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/existential-fallacy/map/o3> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/existential-fallacy/map/ca3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.arg.dundee.ac.uk/aif#CA-node> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/existential-fallacy/map/o1> <http://www.arg.dundee.ac.uk/aif#claimText> "Both premises are rules about whoever beats quota; neither says that anyone did." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/existential-fallacy/map/o1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.arg.dundee.ac.uk/aif#I-node> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/existential-fallacy/map/o2> <http://www.arg.dundee.ac.uk/aif#claimText> "If no one beat quota this quarter, both premises are true and the conclusion is false." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/existential-fallacy/map/o2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.arg.dundee.ac.uk/aif#I-node> .
