  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/existential-fallacy> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The formal fallacy of drawing a particular conclusion, which asserts that something exists, from universal premises that do not assert that their subject class has any members; under the modern (Boolean) reading of categorical propositions, a syllogism with two universal premises and a particular conclusion is invalid unless an existence premise is added." .
