  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/fallacy-of-four-terms> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The syllogistic fallacy of an argument that looks like a categorical syllogism but uses four terms instead of three, usually because one word carries two meanings, so the middle term never actually links the subject and predicate of the conclusion." .
