  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/undistributed-middle> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The syllogistic fallacy committed when the middle term, the term shared by both premises, is not distributed in either premise, so each premise may be about a different part of its class and nothing links the conclusion's two terms." .
