  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/de-re-de-dicto-distinction> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "De re/de dicto distinction" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/de-re-de-dicto-distinction> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "de re and de dicto readings" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/de-re-de-dicto-distinction> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "relational/notional distinction" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/de-re-de-dicto-distinction> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "wide-scope/narrow-scope reading of attitude reports" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/de-re-de-dicto-distinction> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/predicate-logic> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/de-re-de-dicto-distinction> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The practice of separating two readings of a belief, knowledge or modal claim: de dicto, about how the subject thinks of or describes something (the term stays inside the \"that\"-clause), and de re, about the thing itself however it is described (the term takes wide scope). Fixing the reading shows when swapping co-referring terms is licensed." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/de-re-de-dicto-distinction> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/scheme/formal-logic> .
