  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/existential-import> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The property a statement has when its truth requires that something exists, typically that its subject class has at least one member; logicians disagree about which categorical forms (A, E, I, O) carry it, and the answer decides which traditional immediate inferences and syllogisms count as valid." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/existential-import> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/scheme/formal-logic> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/existential-import> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Existential import" .
