  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/possible-worlds-semantics> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A way of evaluating claims about necessity and possibility by treating \"necessarily A\" as A being true in every accessible possible world and \"possibly A\" as A being true in at least one; used as a test, it builds a small model of worlds in which a modal argument's premises hold and its conclusion fails." .
