  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/stoic-logic> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The logic developed by the Stoic school of ancient Greece, above all by Chrysippus (3rd century BCE): a system of whole propositions joined by connectives such as \"if\", \"or\", \"and\" and \"not\", with five basic argument forms (the indemonstrables) and rules for reducing other arguments to them; it is the earliest substantial forerunner of modern propositional logic." .
