  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/necessary-and-sufficient-conditions> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Necessary and sufficient conditions" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/necessary-and-sufficient-conditions> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "jointly sufficient conditions" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/necessary-and-sufficient-conditions> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "necessary condition" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/necessary-and-sufficient-conditions> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "necessity and sufficiency" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/necessary-and-sufficient-conditions> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "sufficient condition" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/necessary-and-sufficient-conditions> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/conditional-statement> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/necessary-and-sufficient-conditions> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A necessary condition for Y is one without which Y cannot hold; a sufficient condition for Y is one whose presence guarantees Y. In a true conditional \"if P then Q\", P is sufficient for Q and Q is necessary for P." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/necessary-and-sufficient-conditions> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/scheme/foundations> .
