<https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/affect-heuristic#graph> {
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/affect-heuristic> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2026-11-08"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/affect-heuristic> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/ontology#Heuristic> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/affect-heuristic> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Affect heuristic" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/affect-heuristic> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "affect-as-information heuristic" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/affect-heuristic> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "risk-as-feelings shortcut" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/affect-heuristic> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/heuristic> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/affect-heuristic> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The mental shortcut of judging risks, benefits and choices by the quick, often automatic feeling of goodness or badness a thing evokes, which makes perceived risk and perceived benefit move in opposite directions even when in reality they are independent or positively related." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/affect-heuristic> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/scheme/heuristics-and-dual-process> .
