  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/bounded-rationality> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The idea, introduced by Herbert Simon, that real decision makers reason within limits of information, time and computational capacity, so their rationality is better described by good-enough search and stopping rules than by the global optimization of the idealised \"economic man\"." .
