  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/dual-process-theory> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The family of theories holding that judgment and reasoning draw on two kinds of processing: fast, autonomous Type 1 processes that supply default answers, and slower, working-memory-dependent Type 2 processes that can reflect on, test and sometimes override those defaults." .
