  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/fast-and-frugal-heuristics> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The research program, launched by Gerd Gigerenzer and colleagues in the mid-1990s, that models judgment as the use of simple, precisely specified rules which search little information, stop early and decide on one or a few cues, and that judges such rules by how well they fit the structure of the environment rather than by logical or statistical norms." .
