  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/satisficing> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A decision strategy, named by Herbert Simon in 1956, in which options are examined one at a time and search stops at the first option that meets a preset aspiration level, with the aspiration raised or lowered according to how easy satisfactory options prove to find." .
