  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/aristotles-rhetoric> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Aristotle's three-book treatise (4th century BCE) defining rhetoric as the ability to see the available means of persuasion in a case. It names three kinds of proof (the speaker's character, the audience's emotions and the argument itself) and treats argument through two rhetorical counterparts of logic: the enthymeme for deduction and the example (paradeigma) for induction, the first systematic account of arguing from one similar case to another." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/aristotles-rhetoric> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/scheme/history-and-thinkers> .
