  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/charles-hamblin> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Australian philosopher and computer pioneer (1922-1985) whose book Fallacies (1970) attacked the textbook \"standard treatment\" of fallacies and proposed formal dialectic, rule-governed dialogue games with commitment stores, as the proper framework for studying them, helping launch modern informal logic and formal argumentation." .
