  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/gerd-gigerenzer> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Psychologist and long-time Max Planck director who argued that simple, fast-and-frugal heuristics can be ecologically rational rather than error-prone, showed that natural frequencies improve Bayesian reasoning, and became the leading critic of the heuristics-and-biases program and an advocate of risk literacy." .
