  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/john-buridan> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Fourteenth-century Paris arts master (c. 1300-c. 1360) and the leading logician of the later Middle Ages, who recast the syllogism as a kind of formal consequence, gave the classic rules for which terms a proposition distributes, and rejected premise pairs whose middle term is never distributed." .
