  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/john-venn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "English logician and Cambridge don (1834-1923) who formalised the overlapping-circle diagrams that now bear his name, read universal propositions as making no claim that anything exists (so subalternation and weakened syllogisms fail), and was a founder of the frequency interpretation of probability in The Logic of Chance (1866)." .
