  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/minna-cheves-wilkins> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Experimental psychologist whose 1928 Archives of Psychology monograph on syllogistic reasoning is the earliest study routinely cited for content and belief effects in deduction: the same logical form was handled differently depending on whether it was stated in familiar, symbolic or belief-conflicting terms." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/minna-cheves-wilkins> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/scheme/history-and-thinkers> .
