<https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/prior-analytics#graph> {
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/prior-analytics> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2026-11-04"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/prior-analytics> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/ontology#Work> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/prior-analytics> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Prior Analytics" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/prior-analytics> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Analytica Priora" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/prior-analytics> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Aristotle's syllogistic treatise" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/prior-analytics> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/organon> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/prior-analytics> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Aristotle's two-book treatise (c. 350 BCE) that founded formal logic: it classifies two-premise deductions into three figures, proves the imperfect ones by reducing them to a handful of self-evident first-figure moods, shows invalidity by counterexample, and extends the system to necessity and possibility." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/prior-analytics> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/scheme/history-and-thinkers> .
