  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/richard-larrick> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "American decision researcher at Duke University's Fuqua School of Business who, as a Michigan graduate student with Richard Nisbett, showed in 1990 that brief training in cost-benefit rules reduces sunk cost reasoning, later sorted debiasing methods into motivational, cognitive and technological strategies, and identified the MPG illusion and people's misappreciation of averaging opinions." .
