  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/theaetetus> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Plato's dialogue (about 369 BCE) in which Socrates and the young mathematician Theaetetus test three definitions of knowledge (perception, true judgement, and true judgement with an account) and reject all three; its last proposal is the usual ancestor cited for the justified-true-belief analysis of knowledge." .
