<https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/ad-hominem#graph> {
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/ad-hominem/cq/1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/ontology#CriticalQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/ad-hominem/cq/1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "How well is the allegation about the person actually supported by evidence?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/ad-hominem/cq/1> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/ad-hominem> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/ad-hominem/cq/2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/ontology#CriticalQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/ad-hominem/cq/2> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Does the person's character, interest or conduct matter in this kind of exchange, for example because we are relying on their testimony or judgment?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/ad-hominem/cq/2> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/ad-hominem> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/ad-hominem/cq/3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/ontology#CriticalQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/ad-hominem/cq/3> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Would the argument still stand if someone with no stake in it had made it?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/ad-hominem/cq/3> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/ad-hominem> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/ad-hominem/cq/4> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/ontology#CriticalQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/ad-hominem/cq/4> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Is the attack used to lower the weight we give the speaker's say-so, or to declare the claim itself false?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/ad-hominem/cq/4> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/ad-hominem> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/ad-hominem/cq/5> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/ontology#CriticalQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/ad-hominem/cq/5> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Could the apparent bias or inconsistency be explained once the person is allowed to respond?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/ad-hominem/cq/5> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/ad-hominem> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/ad-hominem/map/c> <http://www.arg.dundee.ac.uk/aif#claimText> "So the recommendation is wrong and the comparison can be ignored." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/ad-hominem/map/c> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.arg.dundee.ac.uk/aif#I-node> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/ad-hominem/map/ca1> <http://www.arg.dundee.ac.uk/aif#Conclusion> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/ad-hominem/map/ra> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/ad-hominem/map/ca1> <http://www.arg.dundee.ac.uk/aif#Premise> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/ad-hominem/map/o1> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/ad-hominem/map/ca1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.arg.dundee.ac.uk/aif#CA-node> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/ad-hominem/map/ca2> <http://www.arg.dundee.ac.uk/aif#Conclusion> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/ad-hominem/map/ra> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/ad-hominem/map/ca2> <http://www.arg.dundee.ac.uk/aif#Premise> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/ad-hominem/map/o2> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/ad-hominem/map/ca2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.arg.dundee.ac.uk/aif#CA-node> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/ad-hominem/map/o1> <http://www.arg.dundee.ac.uk/aif#claimText> "The past job is a fair reason to check the cost comparison closely, not a reason to think its figures are false." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/ad-hominem/map/o1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.arg.dundee.ac.uk/aif#I-node> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/ad-hominem/map/o2> <http://www.arg.dundee.ac.uk/aif#claimText> "The comparison's numbers can be verified independently of who compiled them." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/ad-hominem/map/o2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.arg.dundee.ac.uk/aif#I-node> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/ad-hominem/map/p1> <http://www.arg.dundee.ac.uk/aif#claimText> "A procurement analyst recommends switching to a cheaper cloud-storage vendor, backed by a cost comparison." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/ad-hominem/map/p1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.arg.dundee.ac.uk/aif#I-node> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/ad-hominem/map/p2> <http://www.arg.dundee.ac.uk/aif#claimText> "The analyst used to work for that vendor." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/ad-hominem/map/p2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.arg.dundee.ac.uk/aif#I-node> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/ad-hominem/map/ra> <http://www.arg.dundee.ac.uk/aif#Conclusion> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/ad-hominem/map/c> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/ad-hominem/map/ra> <http://www.arg.dundee.ac.uk/aif#Premise> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/ad-hominem/map/p1> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/ad-hominem/map/ra> <http://www.arg.dundee.ac.uk/aif#Premise> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/ad-hominem/map/p2> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/ad-hominem/map/ra> <http://www.arg.dundee.ac.uk/aif#partOf> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/ad-hominem/map> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/ad-hominem/map/ra> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.arg.dundee.ac.uk/aif#RA-node> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/ad-hominem/map> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.arg.dundee.ac.uk/aif#ArgumentNetwork> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/ad-hominem/map> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/ontology#illustrates> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/ad-hominem> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/ad-hominem/map> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/ontology#verdict> "fallacious" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/ad-hominem> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2026-11-06"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/ad-hominem> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/ontology#InformalFallacy> .
