<https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/false-dilemma#graph> {
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/false-dilemma/cq/1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/ontology#CriticalQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/false-dilemma/cq/1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Are the options offered really the only ones, or has a third course, a compromise or a combination been left out?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/false-dilemma/cq/1> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/false-dilemma> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/false-dilemma/cq/2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/ontology#CriticalQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/false-dilemma/cq/2> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Are the options actually mutually exclusive, or could both be pursued at once?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/false-dilemma/cq/2> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/false-dilemma> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/false-dilemma/cq/3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/ontology#CriticalQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/false-dilemma/cq/3> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Do the bad consequences attached to the rejected option really follow from it?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/false-dilemma/cq/3> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/false-dilemma> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/false-dilemma/cq/4> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/ontology#CriticalQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/false-dilemma/cq/4> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Who framed the choice, and would they benefit if the unlisted options stayed off the table?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/false-dilemma/cq/4> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/false-dilemma> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/false-dilemma/map/c> <http://www.arg.dundee.ac.uk/aif#claimText> "So our customer satisfaction scores will collapse." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/false-dilemma/map/c> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.arg.dundee.ac.uk/aif#I-node> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/false-dilemma/map/ca1> <http://www.arg.dundee.ac.uk/aif#Conclusion> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/false-dilemma/map/ra> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/false-dilemma/map/ca1> <http://www.arg.dundee.ac.uk/aif#Premise> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/false-dilemma/map/o1> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/false-dilemma/map/ca1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.arg.dundee.ac.uk/aif#CA-node> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/false-dilemma/map/ca2> <http://www.arg.dundee.ac.uk/aif#Conclusion> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/false-dilemma/map/ra> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/false-dilemma/map/ca2> <http://www.arg.dundee.ac.uk/aif#Premise> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/false-dilemma/map/o2> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/false-dilemma/map/ca2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.arg.dundee.ac.uk/aif#CA-node> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/false-dilemma/map/o1> <http://www.arg.dundee.ac.uk/aif#claimText> "The team could add a self-service help page, reroute simple tickets, or hire one part-time agent; the either-or premise omits these." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/false-dilemma/map/o1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.arg.dundee.ac.uk/aif#I-node> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/false-dilemma/map/o2> <http://www.arg.dundee.ac.uk/aif#claimText> "Satisfaction might be protected by fixing the product issues that generate most tickets, which neither option addresses." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/false-dilemma/map/o2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.arg.dundee.ac.uk/aif#I-node> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/false-dilemma/map/p1> <http://www.arg.dundee.ac.uk/aif#claimText> "Either we hire two more support agents this quarter or our customer satisfaction scores will collapse." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/false-dilemma/map/p1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.arg.dundee.ac.uk/aif#I-node> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/false-dilemma/map/p2> <http://www.arg.dundee.ac.uk/aif#claimText> "We cannot afford two more agents this quarter." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/false-dilemma/map/p2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.arg.dundee.ac.uk/aif#I-node> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/false-dilemma/map/ra> <http://www.arg.dundee.ac.uk/aif#Conclusion> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/false-dilemma/map/c> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/false-dilemma/map/ra> <http://www.arg.dundee.ac.uk/aif#Premise> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/false-dilemma/map/p1> .
