  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/slippery-slope> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "An argument that a proposed first step should be rejected because it would set off a chain of further steps ending in an unacceptable outcome; it is fallacious when the chain, the point of no return or the outcome's likelihood is asserted rather than supported." .
