  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/philosophical-skepticism> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The family of philosophical positions and arguments holding that we lack knowledge (or justified belief) in some domain where we ordinarily claim it, so that suspending judgment is the only fully warranted attitude; it ranges from local doubts about induction or the external world to the ancient Pyrrhonian suspension of all belief." .
