  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/sorites-paradox> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "little-by-little argument" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/sorites-paradox> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "paradox of the heap" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/sorites-paradox> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/paradox> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/sorites-paradox> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The ancient puzzle in which a chain of individually plausible small steps (\"removing one grain cannot turn a heap into a non-heap\") leads by valid reasoning from a clearly true starting point to a clearly false conclusion; it arises from tolerant, vague predicates and tests how logic should handle borderline cases." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/sorites-paradox> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/scheme/philosophy-of-reasoning> .
