  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/vagueness> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The property of a word or claim that has borderline cases, where it is unclear whether it applies, such as \"bald\", \"tall\", \"poor\" or \"likely\"; unlike ambiguity it involves one fuzzy meaning rather than several distinct ones, and it is what generates the sorites paradox and line-drawing disputes." .
