<https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/conjunction-fallacy#graph> {
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/conjunction-fallacy/cq/1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/ontology#CriticalQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/conjunction-fallacy/cq/1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Is the detailed version of the claim really more likely than the shorter claim it contains?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/conjunction-fallacy/cq/1> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/conjunction-fallacy> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/conjunction-fallacy/cq/2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/ontology#CriticalQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/conjunction-fallacy/cq/2> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "If I strip out the extra detail, does every case that fits the detailed story still fit the short one?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/conjunction-fallacy/cq/2> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/conjunction-fallacy> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/conjunction-fallacy/cq/3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/ontology#CriticalQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/conjunction-fallacy/cq/3> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Out of 100 comparable cases, how many would show A, and how many of those would also show B?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/conjunction-fallacy/cq/3> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/conjunction-fallacy> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/conjunction-fallacy/cq/4> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/ontology#CriticalQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/conjunction-fallacy/cq/4> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Am I rating how plausible or coherent the story sounds rather than how often it would happen?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/conjunction-fallacy/cq/4> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/conjunction-fallacy> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/conjunction-fallacy/map/c> <http://www.arg.dundee.ac.uk/aif#claimText> "The vendor is more likely to go bankrupt because its supplier fails than to go bankrupt at all, so we should budget for the first risk and not the second." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/conjunction-fallacy/map/c> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.arg.dundee.ac.uk/aif#I-node> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/conjunction-fallacy/map/ca1> <http://www.arg.dundee.ac.uk/aif#Conclusion> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/conjunction-fallacy/map/ra> .
