  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/gamblers-fallacy> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "fallacy of the maturity of chances" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/gamblers-fallacy> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "negative recency bias" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/gamblers-fallacy> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/probabilistic-fallacy> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/gamblers-fallacy> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The mistaken belief that, in a sequence of independent random events, an outcome becomes less likely after it has occurred several times in a row (or \"due\" after it has not), as if chance corrected itself in the short run." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/gamblers-fallacy> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/scheme/probabilistic-reasoning> .
