  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/law-of-small-numbers> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The mistaken intuition, named by Tversky and Kahneman in 1971, that even a small random sample will closely resemble the population it came from, so that small-sample results look more stable, more conclusive and more likely to replicate than sampling theory allows." .
