  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/correlation-versus-causation> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The principle that a statistical association between two variables does not by itself show that one causes the other, because the pattern can also arise from a common cause, reverse causation, selection of the sample, or chance; causal conclusions need further evidence and explicit assumptions." .
