<https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/researcher-degrees-of-freedom#graph> {
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/researcher-degrees-of-freedom> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2026-11-07"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/researcher-degrees-of-freedom> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/ontology#Concept> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/researcher-degrees-of-freedom> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Researcher degrees of freedom" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/researcher-degrees-of-freedom> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "analytic flexibility" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/researcher-degrees-of-freedom> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "garden of forking paths" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/researcher-degrees-of-freedom> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "undisclosed flexibility" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/researcher-degrees-of-freedom> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/scientific-method> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/researcher-degrees-of-freedom> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/statistical-reasoning> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/researcher-degrees-of-freedom> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The many often-arbitrary choices a researcher makes in framing hypotheses, designing a study, collecting and analysing data and reporting results; when those choices are made after seeing the data, or left undisclosed, they can make a false hypothesis look statistically significant." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/researcher-degrees-of-freedom> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/scheme/scientific-reasoning> .
